@startuml

'==== Title ====
title "As a User, I want to use the Web UI to sort the list of publications in my library by title, author, type or ISBN/ISSN." - SD Level 2

'==== basic style ====
skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName Futura
skinparam objectFontSize 20
skinparam backgroundColor CornSilk
skinparam objectBackgroundColor WhiteSmoke
skinparam noteBackgroundColor #FFFFE0
skinparam ArrowFontColor #3B4953
skinparam ActivationBackgroundColor black
hidefootbox
autonumber

actor User as USER
participant ":Frontend" as FRONTEND
participant ":Backend" as rest
participant ":Database" as DB

note over FRONTEND
  Assumes the User already opened or accessed My Library,
  and that the frontend discovered the available library actions
  through OPTIONS /my-library.

  The frontend follows the library href and applies
  the selected sort criterion instead of using a hardcoded URL.
end note

USER -> FRONTEND : I want to sort the publications in my library by title, author, type or ISBN/ISSN.
activate FRONTEND

note over FRONTEND
Supported sort criteria:
- title
- author
- type
- identifier (ISBN/ISSN)
end note

FRONTEND -> rest : GET {library href expanded with sort={field}}\nX-User-Id: {email}
activate rest

rest -> DB : FETCH library item details
activate DB
DB --> rest : DATA
deactivate DB

rest --> FRONTEND : 200 OK + LibraryItemResponseDTO list\n+ links
deactivate rest

FRONTEND --> USER : Display sorted publications in my library.
deactivate FRONTEND

@enduml